The flag is **`-a`** (or `--handle`). When you use it, nft will include the rule handle in the output, e.g.:

```bash
nft list ruleset -a
```

Output example:
```
table ip filter {
    chain input {
        type filter hook input priority filter; policy accept;
        handle 1  ip saddr 192.168.0.0/24 accept
        handle 2  ip saddr 10.0.0.0/8 accept
    }
}
```

